  "helpScreenMessageSettingsProfilesTitle": "Settings profiles",
  "helpScreenMessageSettingsProfilesContent": "Settings profiles allow you to save and quickly restore application configuration. You can create multiple profiles with different recording and screen settings, then switch between them.\n\nEach profile contains:\n• Recording settings ($[recordingInputDevice]input device, $[recordingAudioEncoder]codec, $[recordingSampleRate]sample rate, $[recordingBitRate]bit rate, $[recordingAudioMode]audio mode, $[recordingAutoGain]automatic gain, $[recordingEchoCancel]echo cancellation, $[recordingNoiseSuppress]noise suppression)\n• Screen settings ($[language]language, $[screenThemeMode]theme, $[screenThemeColor]accent color, $[keepScreenOn]keep screen on)\n\nTo create a profile, use the $[create]\"Create\" button in the profiles dialog. To load a profile, tap it. To delete a profile, $[touchLong]long-press it and select the $[deleteForever]delete option.",
  "projectExportInfo": "Project export saves all recordings and their parameters to a ZIP file that can be loaded later. Project name is optional and will be added to the file name.",
  "settingsProfilesInfo": "Save and restore application configuration. Tap to load a profile, or long-press to see details.",
  "moreSettings": "More settings...",
  "help": "Help",
  "helpScreenMessageAboutTitle": "About",
  "helpScreenMessageAboutContent": "This application lets you record audio from a\u00A0microphone or USB audio interface (your device must support USB OTG) to one of several tracks. You can also import an existing audio file.\n\nRecordings can play in sync (all tracks together) or independently, in a\u00A0loop or once.\n\nRecordings and their settings, plus the UI theme and language, are remembered after you close the app.",
  "helpScreenMessageGridScreenTitle": "Tracks grid screen",
  "helpScreenMessageGridScreenContent": "Short press a\u00A0colored track block or use a\u00A0hotkey (visible at the top of the track) to perform one of the available actions.\n\nHold the track block or use a\u00A0hotkey with a modifier key (usually Control $[controlKey], often Command on Mac) to open track details.\n\nIn the drawer you can choose the keyboard mode (standard or 24-key pad). Set each track’s hotkey in that track’s details.",
  "helpScreenMessageDetailsScreenTitle": "Track details screen",
  "helpScreenMessageDetailsScreenContent": "Main track settings:\n• $[recordingClip]recording trim\n• $[trackPlaybackMode]playback mode\n• $[trackPlaybackVolume]playback volume\n• $[trackPlaybackBalance]audio balance\n• $[trackPlaybackSpeed]playback speed\n• $[trackName]track name\n• $[trackKeyboardKey]keyboard shortcut\n\nYou can also $[trackRecordingMove]move the track on the grid, $[trackRecordingImport]import a recording file, $[trackRecordingShare]share the recording, or $[deleteForever]delete it.",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackStates": "Track states and actions",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackStatesInfo": "Each track can be in one of several states that determine available actions. Tapping the track block runs the action for the current state.",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackIcons": "Track info icons",
  "helpScreenMessageTrackIconsInfo": "Icons displayed on the track block inform about its properties.",
  "helpTrackIconBalanceLeftLegend": "panned left; exact mix in track details",
  "helpTrackIconBalanceCenterLegend": "balance centered",
  "helpTrackIconBalanceRightLegend": "panned right; exact mix in track details",
  "helpTrackIconPlaybackStartTrimLegend": "trimmed at the start; exact time in track details",
  "helpTrackIconPlaybackEndTrimLegend": "trimmed at the end; exact time in track details",
  "helpTrackIconSinglePlaybackModeLegend": "plays once, then stops",
  "helpTrackIconRepeatPlaybackModeLegend": "loops back to the range start",
  "helpScreenMessageSettingsInfo": "Here you can set $[recordingAudioEncoder]audio codec, $[recordingSampleRate]sample rate, $[recordingBitRate]bit rate, $[recordingAudioMode]audio mode, $[recordingAutoGain]automatic gain, $[recordingEchoCancel]echo cancellation, and $[recordingNoiseSuppress]noise suppression.",
  "helpScreenMessageProjectExportImportTitle": "Project export and import",
  "helpScreenMessageProjectExportImportContent": "You can $[projectExport]save the entire project to a\u00A0ZIP file, which contains grid settings, all tracks with their settings, and audio recordings. The file can later be $[projectImport]loaded to restore the entire application state.\n\nThe exported file contains:\n• Grid settings (number of rows and columns)\n• All track settings (names, playback parameters, playback trim, keyboard shortcuts)\n• All audio recordings with checksums\n• Project metadata (version, export date, statistics)\n\nBefore import, a\u00A0project preview is displayed, and the application warns about overwriting the current session. Import performs full validation before modifying data.",
